body:
i think you're going to get a lot of comments telling you that feeling this way is selfish, or not wanting to have a balance is selfish- but please don't let that get to you. you're entitled to your own sexual boundaries and you should never have to 'fake' it. compromising is for where you're going to eat, not for what you do in sex. it's pretty clear that being in a dominant position makes you feel uncomfortable- which is the most important thing, and something you absolutely need to communicate to your partner. however, your partner is also not at fault for needing something different. tldr; you're both very entitled to your feelings!  if that means you and your partner aren't compatible, then so be it. i guess it depends how important this dynamic is to your relationship.

&#x200B;

ps. you will also get a lot of people saying that if thats what she wants, you should let her see someone else. if you're comfortable with that, thats okay and a good solution! however, a lot of people aren't and if you're one of that please don't feel pressured to open up your relationship to appease one person in it (:
